{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117385","id":3393663765,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7KRzMV","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117385","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117385.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117385.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117385","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117385/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117385/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117385/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/eb680bc8c3e4a811dc8736716fd9cf57567c21dd","number":117385,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Wayland: Improve mapping robustness and synchronization","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #115739.\r\nShould fix #104752. (Didn't replicate on any of my usual compositors)\r\n\r\nWe assumed that a window will be ready after a single roundtrip but that's actually not guaranteed by the XDG shell protocol.\r\n\r\nThis patch waits for an arbitrary timeout (10s) before erroring out and forcefully closing the window. Since this exercised quite some code paths, it also reworks some window handling logic and fixes a bunch of synchronization issues.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTested with Pinnacle 0.2.2 (built from commit `b6c40da68024fb7fbb1db1f0890a87b08da013c9`) on my KISS Linux laptop by following the steps from the [linked issue](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115739). Couldn't notice any obvious regression on my KISS Linux laptop with sway 1.11 and my Fedora 43 VM with KDE 6.5.4, GNOME 49.2.2, and COSMIC 1.0.1.\r\n\r\nNote that this solution isn't ideal as the world stops while waiting. We should obviously make everything asynchronous but I'm not entirely sure how much that is possible.\r\n\r\nIf the timed out window is the main window the engine will fall back to X11 properly, although for some reason *only in this case* `DetectPrimeX11` (if invoked) stalls. I'd really postpone this issue to another PR if possible, given how specific it is. (Does it even count as a regression? :P)","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097326,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTczMjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:linuxbsd","name":"platform:linuxbsd","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1327318271,"node_id":"MD